 ## Background
-The method was presented in the paper "Multiresolution MIP Rendering of Large Volumetric Data Accelerated on Graphics Hardware" [S1]. It is part of a broader approach to multiresolution volume rendering, specifically focusing on the projection of wavelet detail coefficients [S1]. The technique is designed to handle large volumetric datasets by exploiting the hierarchical nature of wavelet decompositions and accelerating the rendering process using graphics hardware [S1].
+The method is described in the paper "Multiresolution MIP Rendering of Large Volumetric Data Accelerated on Graphics Hardware" (EuroVis 2007) [S1]. It builds on the principles of multiresolution and level of detail, specifically utilizing wavelet-based decomposition for volume rendering [S1, S2]. The approach was developed to address the computational and memory challenges of rendering large volumetric datasets on graphics hardware [S1].
 
